---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About - DataTech Consulting and Contracting"
  description="DataTech is a founder-led technology delivery firm in Columbus, Ohio. We build fixed-scope AI systems for local service businesses and stay on for support after launch."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="page-title">About DataTech</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      DataTech Consulting and Contracting is a founder-led technology delivery
      firm based in Columbus, Ohio. We help local service businesses turn
      missed calls, slow follow-up, and manual paperwork into systems that
      run the same way every day.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>
        We build fixed-scope AI systems: a support assistant that answers and
        captures jobs after hours, lead intake that arrives complete, call
        review that surfaces what needs a person, a knowledge assistant for
        your own team, and document work that removes retyping. Each offer
        has a set scope and a set price, and we support what we build on a
        monthly plan.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our method is plain. Diagnose the workflow first. Name what is
        included and what is not. Build one thing well, test it on your real
        work, hand it over with a guide your staff can follow, then review it
        with you after launch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How the firm is set up</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Founder-led</h3>
          <p>
            Our founder sets the technical direction on every build and
            reviews the scope before work starts. You get senior judgement on
            the decisions that are hard to undo.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Operations-managed</h3>
          <p>
            Delivery is managed day to day: communication, follow-through,
            and the client experience are someone's named job, not an
            afterthought.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Specialist-supported</h3>
          <p>
            When a build needs a skill outside the core team, we bring in a
            specialist for that scope. The firm stays accountable for the
            whole result.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p>
        We describe the firm this way on purpose. We sell DataTech, not one
        person's calendar. Founder involvement is a strength, and we frame it
        as oversight and direction, not as the whole delivery plan.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we work with clients</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Company-first.</strong> Every proposal names the firm, the roles, and the method, not a resume.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed scope, written down.</strong> Deliverables, limits, and acceptance are agreed before we build.</li>
        <li><strong>Human approval where it matters.</strong> Our systems escalate to a person instead of guessing on anything outside the approved scope.</li>
        <li><strong>Proof from real work.</strong> We publish work we own and operate, and client work only with permission. See the <a href="/proof/">proof page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Support after launch.</strong> A build is not done at handover. Monthly support covers monitoring, updates, and small fixes.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Start a conversation</h2>
      <p>
        If your business loses work to missed calls, slow follow-up, or
        paperwork your team retypes by hand, a 20-minute fit call is the
        place to start. We will tell you on the call if we are not the right
        firm for it.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a fit call</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
